SUMMARY:Practicing the Lost Art of Friendly Disagreement
DESCRIPTION:Practising the Lost Art of Friendly Disagreement — Social Club 150 hosts Dr. Fiona MacDonald\, Associate Professor of Political Science and polarization expert at the University of Northern British Columbia\, for a talk on staying connected across differing opinions — at home\, at work\, and online. Wednesday\, September 2\, 6:45–8:45pm\, East End Chapter\, 765 Queen St E. Open to everyone; $20 for non-members. Register at socialclub150.com.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/practicing-the-lost-art-of-friendly-disagreement/
LOCATION:Ralph Thornton Community Centre\, 765 Queen Street East\, Toronto\, M4M 1H3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://d28bcn7yu97icd.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/14143846/IG-Post-Friendly-Disagreement.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Social Club 150":MAILTO:150@socialclub150.com
END:VEVENT
